     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi all -<div><br></div><div>I was wondering if anyone knew an easy solution to this problem instead of the rig below.  The problem is fairly evident from the comments -</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">df</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#000000\">data.frame</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span> = <span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:#224f1e\">5</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">y</span> = <span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:#224f1e\">5</span>)</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147);min-height:16px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># i want to be able to easily see the color in the legend in the below plot</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># i.e., make the points in the legend big, while those in the plot are small</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\">qplot<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>y<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>data<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>df<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>colour<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>size<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>I<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">))</span></div><p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px;font:12.0px Monaco;color:#001b93;min-height:16.0px\">  <br></p><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># this works... </div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">ggplot</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">aes</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span> = <span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">y</span> = <span style=\"color:#000000\">y</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">colour</span> = <span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>, <span style=\"color:#000000\">size</span> = <span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span>), <span style=\"color:#000000\">data</span> = <span style=\"color:#000000\">df</span>) + </div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>geom_point<span style=\"color:#001b93\">() +</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>scale_size<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>legend<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#b98a23\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">)</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(0,27,147);min-height:16px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># ...but i need this construction...</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\">ggplot<span style=\"color:#001b93\">() + </span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>geom_point<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>aes<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>y<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>y<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>colour<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\">, </span>size<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">0</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">*</span>x<span style=\"color:#001b93\">+</span><span style=\"color:#224f1e\">1</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">), </span>data<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span>df<span style=\"color:#001b93\">) +</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco\"><span style=\"color:#001b93\">  </span>scale_size<span style=\"color:#001b93\">(</span>legend<span style=\"color:#001b93\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#b98a23\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#001b93\">)    </span></div><p style=\"margin:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px;font:12.0px Monaco;color:#001b93;min-height:16.0px\">  <br></p><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># surely there&#39;s an easier way to do this? i.e., without creating a bogus</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># function of one of the variables?</div></div><div><br></div><div>Ideas?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>david.</div><div><br><div> <div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:norma